# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose.
#
# These were `dist/` and `build/`, which git matches against a directory of that
# name at ANY depth. That quietly swallowed `apps/web/src/app/(site)/build` and
# `apps/web/src/components/build` — the agent sketchpad and its eight
# components. Two things broke and neither announced itself: the files would
# never have been committed, and Tailwind v4's automatic source detection skips
# ignored paths, so not one class in that directory was ever compiled and the
# page rendered unstyled with no error anywhere.
#
# The Python artefacts these were written for are produced at the root, so
# anchoring costs nothing. If a package ever needs its own ignored build output,
# give it its own anchored path rather than reintroducing a bare pattern.
/dist/
/build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

